session 2026-08-26 (6) — "FUCKING FINISH ROADMAP", THIRTEENTH SESSION, SECOND HALF: F6 pause/resume, O10(a), O6's ladder, O4-polish closed, O8b, O9, F8 closed — and the map is now empty of buildable work. (1) F6 PAUSE/RESUME SHIPPED. The segment machinery was already there (a kind has been able to be several non-overlapping ChannelRecordings since 08-23), so what F6 adds is the one thing setChannelActive could not do: hold the take WITHOUT RELEASING ANYTHING. pause() closes each live channel's current segment and keeps its track; resume() opens segment N+1 on the same track with no prompt and no picker. THE PAUSE IS EXCLUDED BY MOVING THE SESSION EPOCH forward by the gap, which is one line and makes every startOffsetMs downstream correct at once — closed segments keep their offsets, the next lands where the last ended, and the elapsed counter stops counting time nobody recorded. The composite is CANCELLED at the pause rather than marked, because it is one continuous file whose timestamps are arrivals and cannot represent a gap; a paused take therefore exports through the render, the same fallback a late join takes. Verified on the DEPLOYED build: 8 segments, seams 99/101/207/218 ms, 17,345 ms of recorded material from a longer wall clock, composite absent. RETAKE IS NOT BUILT and is scoped rather than half-done: it is not a capture feature at all but a resume of a FINISHED recording, touching recovery, editsRepo and editor state. (2) O10(a): THE MEASUREMENT JUSTIFIES THE TASK AND THEN THE MODE DOES NOTHING, WHICH IS THE FINDING. The shipped p90-window-RMS makeup lands three content shapes 7.84 dB apart (speech -13.08 LUFS, bass -10.20, bright -5.24) — an offset can be dialled in, a spread cannot. Built compose/lufs.ts (BS.1770-4, 14 tests, calibrated to the standard's own 1 kHz reference to 0.15 dB, streaming so a 30-minute take costs one number per 100 ms rather than 690 MB of PCM). Wired ?loudness=r128 end to end. It produces IDENTICAL files, because every shape a