session 2026-08-29 (3) — THE EXPORT TARGETS A QUALITY, NOT A BITRATE, ON ROBERT'S GO ("we need more quality and much less size, its non editable video, movies files with much better quality is twice smaller usually"). X15(a) had already found the lever and left it on the floor: bitrateMode constant/variable are INERT here (byte-identical files, hardware encoder and software both — isConfigSupported accepts a value the encoder ignores), while 'quantizer' IS honoured. It was unreachable through mediabunny, whose bitrateMode is typed 'constant'|'variable' and which never sets the per-frame `quantizer` that the mode also requires. So the encoder is ours for the render path only, via registerEncoder, with the muxer, canvas pump, packet accounting and every fallback untouched. Selection carries NO global state: onEncoderConfig runs before the custom encoder is chosen, so the render stamps its own config object and supports() reads the mark off that very object — two concurrent exports cannot cross.
