LEVEL 4.2, which `isConfigSupported` REFUSES above 1080p rather than clamping, so the size was never a
choice, it was the only size that codec string allows. And Mpx/s is not a machine constant: same
machine, same 40-frame meter, the take's own codec ladder, 3 reps each — 1920x1080 330 · 2560x1662 389
· 3024x1964 398/406/412 · 3840x2160 417. It RISES with frame size (rate.ts's own 2026-08-30 numbers,
362/410/416/435, said the same and were read as noise). 3024x1964@60 wants 356; the machine gives ~405
